well tourism is certainly picking up  across the valley and that's stimulating  our economy jeremy j ford spoke to a  unlv professor to find out how those out  of town dollars are still needed  each day thousands of travelers make  their way through las vegas either  flying via harry reid international or  driving in from neighboring states las  vegas as it has been for a long time is  still a great place to visit there's a  lot of stuff to do here  and people are still really attracted to  vegas as a tourist destination  david g schwartz is a gaming historian  at unlv he tells me we've still got a  long way to go before we reach  pre-pandemic visitor numbers well  obviously with the pandemic there's a  lot less travel people wouldn't come to  las vegas because they couldn't do a lot  of things they wanted to do now a lot of  those restrictions have gone away but we  still have things like high fuel prices  and inflation to deal with which might  cause for some travelers to simply just  stay at home yet some industries in town  are thriving for gaming things are  getting a lot better the gaming revenues  continue to be at record highs we're  seeing the non-gaming pickup  entertainment is starting to come back  so i think the next piece would be  convention as we all wait for things to  be back to normal again i think the most  important thing is that las vegas  economy really is part of the global  economy and we're affected by what  happens around the world jeremy j ford  live local now
 

